WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Hey, welcome to SpaceX Daily, Episode 37.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.700
It's July 19th, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.600
Let's get into today's SpaceX developments.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:12.780
Infrastructure moves in Texas and Louisiana,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.940
plus Falcon's 50th California flight of the year,

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.120
point to concrete steps toward higher launch cadence,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.520
while Starship testing continues.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.180
SpaceX stood down from the planned

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.920
13th integrated flight test of Starship

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.460
after an engine-related condition surfaced

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:30.800
during the terminal count.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.080
The abort came after the vehicle had completed

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.780
full pre-flight sequencing and remained secured

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.920
on the pad at the South Texas site.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.020
Teams identified the issue in the final seconds

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.060
before liftoff and immediately began data review.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.520
The attempt has been rescheduled for July 20

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.300
with the same test objectives,

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.720
while root cause work on the engine anomaly proceeds.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.900
In a separate operation, the same day,

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.600
a Falcon mission successfully delivered satellites

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.500
for the space development agency,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.200
illustrating ongoing separation between the two programs.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.640
SpaceX stood down from Starship's 13th flight test

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.500
after pre-launch checks at the South Texas site.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.700
The vehicle remained on the pad

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.860
while teams assessed the issue that appeared

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.880
in the final moments.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:21.360
This keeps the test campaign on a compressed schedule

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.540
aimed at gathering flight data quickly.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.920
The next attempt will again target

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.380
the same test objectives.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.540
Starship flight 13 ended in an abort

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.020
after an engine issue surfaced on the pad.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.320
The flight test sequence reached the final seconds

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.740
before the hold was called.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.560
root cause work on the engine anomaly

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.680
is now underway ahead of the July 20 retry.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.620
The last second abort of Starship flight 13 occurred

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.280
after the vehicle had completed extensive pre-flight sequencing.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.920
Reports indicate an engine condition triggered the hold

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.400
at the South Texas launch site under the current test campaign.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.500
The outcome is being reviewed

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.220
against the program's rapid iteration targets.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.300
Follow up data from the July 20 attempt

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.340
will clarify whether hardware margins

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.240
align with the planned flight rate.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.740
The Starship test flight was aborted

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:14.880
at the final moment before liftoff.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.680
Teams identified an engine-related condition

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.940
during the terminal count.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.260
The vehicle stayed secured on the pad

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.680
while data review began.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.360
The abort occurred after all prior ground operations

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.900
had completed successfully.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.140
A new target date of July 20 was set following the scrub.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.340
One thing worth watching is whether the July 20 retry

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.120
confirms engine health margins

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.360
that align with the program's rapid iteration targets.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.740
Reports note the vehicle completed extensive pre-flight checks

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.500
yet still encountered the hold,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.920
highlighting the tension between aggressive flight test goals

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.000
and demonstrated engine out tolerance

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.540
ahead of crude missions.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.440
Resolving the root cause and confirming hardware performance

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.420
on the next attempt will show whether the test campaign

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.300
can sustain its intended pace.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.200
While Teams diagnosed the engine issue on the pad,

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.440
longer-term infrastructure work is already underway

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.760
to remove other cadence bottlenecks.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.180
SpaceX is constructing a 13-kilometer pipeline

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.240
in Texas dedicated to supplying propellant directly

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.060
to starbase.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.500
The dedicated line will replace truck deliveries

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.300
and targets higher flight rates

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.440
by moving fuel through a single always ready conduit.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.900
The project runs alongside ongoing gigabay production ramp work

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.220
and will be watched for operational status

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.620
ahead of the next integrated flight tests.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.340
Observers on X noted the rapid rescheduling to July 20

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.980
and discussed how quickly Teams can close out

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.500
the engine anomaly review.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:50.480
While several accounts highlighted the parallel SDA mission

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.580
success as evidence of operational separation,

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.140
the same systems logic behind the Texas pipeline

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.460
also drives plans for a second coastal launch site.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.420
A proposal calls for the Louisiana site

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.280
to serve as the primary starship launch location

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.820
starting in 2028.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.000
The facility would complement Texas operations

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.200
and support higher cadence once orbital refueling

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.740
and booster catch milestones are demonstrated.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.640
Shifting primary flights eastward would reduce pressure

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.060
on the South Texas environmental and regulatory envelope.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.280
Construction timelines and FAA licensing

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.140
remain the next gating items

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.320
and community members tracking infrastructure updates

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.240
pointed to the Louisiana proposal

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.200
as a long-term complement to Texas operations

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.680
once permitting advances.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:40.980
While new sites are planned,

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.320
existing Falcon operations continue

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.220
to deliver the reuse data Starship will need.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.500
SpaceX is preparing its 50th Falcon launch of 2026

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.420
from Vandenberg Space Force Base in California.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.420
The mission continues the site's record cadence

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.820
using reused boosters and fairings.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.520
Each California flight adds data on booster life limits

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.180
and rapid pad recycling.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:07.300
The milestone underscores Falcon 9's role

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.000
in maintaining launch access

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.980
while Starship development proceeds.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.260
Viewers in the region can track live coverage

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.020
through standard public streams.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.560
Arizona residents can view the upcoming Falcon launch

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.360
from Vandenberg via public webcasts

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:23.660
and select ground spots.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.680
The flight adds to the year's California total

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.140
and demonstrates continued reuse of first stage hardware.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.620
Clear weather windows are required

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.560
for visual sightings from the state.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.880
The event provides another data point

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.900
on Falcon turnaround intervals between coastal missions.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.040
From an engineering standpoint,

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.500
the 13 kilometer Texas pipeline under construction

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.320
for star-based propellant delivery

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:50.060
illustrates a classic systems level trade-off

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.680
between logistics overhead and launch cadence.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.280
Trucking liquid oxygen and methane

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.500
to the pad consumes driver hours, vehicle cycles,

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.760
and buffer storage that grows linearly with flight rate.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.180
A fixed pipeline collapses that variable cost

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:07.160
to the marginal energy of pumping

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.980
and removes the throughput limit

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.340
imposed by discrete transport assets

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.320
and the time required to pressurize

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.920
and verify each truckload.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.940
Once the line is online,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.920
the effective idiot index of ground support drops

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.540
because the same propellant mass

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.360
moves through a single conduit

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.660
rather than repeated discrete handoffs.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.960
This change directly supports the open question

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.420
of rapid reuse cadence

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:32.160
by shortening the ground turnaround

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.620
that currently sits between static fire and flight attempts.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:39.220
Next milestones to watch are pressure test results

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.260
and integration with the existing tank farm controls.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.200
The same infrastructure logic applies

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.180
at the proposed Louisiana site.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.160
A dedicated coastal pad removes the need

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.480
to share South Texas airspace and regulatory windows,

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.060
allowing independent flight rate growth

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:59.340
once the first orbital refueling demonstrations succeed.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.660
Shifting primary operations eastward

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.420
also changes the heat shield recovery geometry

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.440
and downrange landing zones,

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.260
which in turn affects booster catch timing

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.300
and tower arm loading profiles.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.820
The engineering decision therefore

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:17.000
trades near-term construction cost

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.620
for long-term parallelism across two

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.560
geographically separated sites.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.380
Listeners following launch infrastructure

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.320
will see the first measurable effect

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.780
when Louisiana permitting filings appear

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.160
and when the Texas pipeline begins

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.020
its own pressure test campaign later this year.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.040
Falcon operations at Vandenberg continue

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.000
to supply the data that validates reuse assumptions

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.280
Starship will later need at scale.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.500
Each of the 50 California flights this year

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.500
recycles the same booster hardware

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.780
through multiple missions,

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:51.560
directly measuring the life limit of engines,

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.880
tanks and grid fins under coastal launch conditions.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.240
That accumulated flight history

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.180
reduces uncertainty in the Starship reuse model

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.440
by providing a real-world baseline for thermal cycling,

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:07.000
propellant loading speed and pad turnaround intervals.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.660
The 50th mission therefore functions

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.640
as both an operational milestone

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.540
and a calibration point for the larger architecture

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.360
still under development in Texas.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.920
Visual observers in Arizona

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.680
shared ground spot recommendations

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.780
for the upcoming Vandenberg flight

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.800
and confirmed clear weather forecasts

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.200
for potential sightings.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.720
Discussions also covered the 13 kilometer pipelines

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.920
potential impact on truck logistics

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:33.860
once it enters service at Starbase.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:39.040
On the AI front, open AI has promoted former XAI engineer

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.320
Uday Rudaraju to CTO of compute,

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.320
moving a key figure with experienced scaling

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:47.960
large training clusters into a senior role

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.240
at a direct competitor.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.800
The appointment underscores the tight talent market

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.860
for high-powered data center architecture

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.100
and the cross pollination between XAI's colossus builds

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.620
and other frontier labs.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:04.460
Rudaraju's prior work on XAI infrastructure

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.780
provides context for how power and networking decisions

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.920
at one site can influence industry-wide approaches,

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.360
though no direct SpaceX hardware tie-in

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.540
is reported in the move and a quick market note.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:22.320
SPCX is trading at $123.99

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.180
down 2.4%.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:27.860
Before we go, watch for pressure test results

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:30.640
on the new Texas pipeline and the first Louisiana

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.640
permitting filings later this year.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.240
That's your SpaceX news for today.

